  "tagline": "Agents that use the browser",
  "description": "Browser Use is the open-source framework that turns website interfaces into structured text so AI agents can navigate the web without fragile vision-only approaches. Founded in 2024 by ETH Zurich graduates Magnus Müller and Gregor Zunic, it came out of Y Combinator's Winter 2025 batch and its MIT-licensed repository is one of the most-starred agent projects on GitHub, at more than 115,000 stars. The company monetises through Browser Use Cloud, a managed service offering stealth browsers, proxies, CAPTCHA solving, and a hosted agent API, and raised a $17 million seed round led by Felicis in March 2025.",
